y can it can  go through the wall which it can quite  easily if there was just one wall a lot  of that thermal energy would be escaping  into the into the surroundings which  mean that's an unwanted energy transfer  be losing lots of that thermal energy  however if I have a cavity installed  there's this air gap in the middle and  the air gap reduces the amount of  thermal energy which is lost to the  external surroundings remember the  thermal conductivity of a gas such as  the air is really low so therefore so  therefore I'll be losing less thermal  energy if I have this cavity between the  inner wall and the outer wall of my  house it also helps to have really thick  walls as well because the thick of the  wall the slower the rate of energy  transfer so guys those are two ways of  reducing unwanted energy transfers  lubrication and insulation thank you
 

